  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.0.0\n\t\t\t- Breaking for every host that implements the storage port: ISecurityAudit has four new optional string properties, OriginIp, ClientAppId, CallerType and TokenId. Your SecurityAudit entity must implement all four, and your database needs four new columns and a migration: OriginIp nvarchar(45), ClientAppId nvarchar(255), CallerType nvarchar(255) and TokenId nvarchar(255), all nullable. Existing rows keep NULL.\n\t\t\t- SecurityAuditClient.LogSecurityAuditAsync and RecordSecurityAuditAsync, the versions that take values, have four new optional parameters, originIp, clientAppId, callerType and tokenId, in that order, after correlationId and before the CancellationToken. Each is copied onto the entry as given. A call that passes the token by position straight after correlationId no longer compiles: name it (cancellationToken: cancellationToken) or pass the new values before it. Recompile anything that calls these methods, and update mock set-ups and verifications of them.\n\t\t\t- OriginIp: the IP address the request came from, IPv4 or IPv6, as text, up to 45 characters (the longest textual form of either). It is personal data, and only as accurate as the host's forwarded-headers setup: behind a proxy, the host must trust and read the forwarded headers or it records the proxy's address. Addresses are not parsed or normalised.\n\t\t\t- ClientAppId, CallerType and TokenId, up to 255 characters each, describe the token the caller presented. With Microsoft Entra ID: ClientAppId is the appid (v1.0) or azp (v2.0) claim, and identifies an app calling as itself; CallerType is free text such as \"Application\" or \"Delegated\", which the library does not interpret; TokenId is the uti claim, which links the entry to the Entra sign-in logs.\n\t\t\t- A security audit that breaks one of these limits is refused on add and modify. Null is allowed for all four.\n\t\t\t- Audits and metrics are unchanged.\n\t\t\t- Upgrade guide: https://github.com/NHSISL/NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics#upgrading-from-03x",
